msgctxt "#30140"
msgid "Enables faster emulation of the PPU at the cost of a minor reduction of accuracy. It is recommended to leave this active."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30141"
msgid "Deinterlaces all games by rendering internally at 480p. Performance penalty is almost non-existent, so it is recommended to leave this active."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30142"
msgid "Removes any limit to the number of sprites that can be drawn simultaneously on screen. May cause issues with certain games."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30143"
msgid "Emulates a bug in older releases of ZSNES and Snes9x, where VRAM blocking was not emulated. A few older ROM hacks relied on this behavior and will render graphics incorrectly if not enabled. This option is extremely inaccurate and hurts PPU speed, so it is recommended to leave it disabled unless you need to play a game that is otherwise incompatible with this core."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30144"
msgid "Enables faster emulation of the DSP at the cost of a minor reduction of accuracy. It is recommended to leave this active."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30145"
msgid "Applies cubic interpolation to the sound, preserving more of the high range."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30146"
msgid "Emulates a bug in ZSNES where echo RAM was treated as separate from APU RAM. Many older ROM hacks for Super Mario World relied on this behavior and will crash without enabling this. This option is extremely inaccurate and should not be enabled unless required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30147"
msgid "Enables faster emulation of the coprocessors at the cost of a minor reduction of accuracy. It is recommended to leave this active."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30148"
msgid "When this option is enabled, less accurate HLE emulation will always be used when available. If disabled, HLE will only be used when LLE firmware is missing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30149"
msgid "Allows to choose the preferred Super Game Boy BIOS to be used with compatible titles. Requires a restart to take effect."
